<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Setup Guide: Relative AAM HovmÃ¶ller</h2>
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Overview of what we're building</h3>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>GitHub repo</strong> (<code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">phillyweatherauthority/philly-weather-tools</code>) hosts the HTML viewer and the Python fetch script + GitHub Action</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>GitHub Action</strong> runs daily, fetches NCEP/NCAR data, writes <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">data/aam_lat_latest.txt</code>, and commits it back</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Netlify</strong> (your existing site) auto-deploys from that repo, so the HTML viewer goes live automatically</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Step 1 â€” Add the files to your repo</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Go to <strong><a class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://github.com/phillyweatherauthority/philly-weather-tools">https://github.com/phillyweatherauthority/philly-weather-tools</a></strong> and add the three files you just downloaded:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>A. The HTML viewer</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">In your repo, click <strong>Add file â†’ Upload files</strong></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Upload <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">aam_hovmoller.html</code> to the <strong>root</strong> of the repo (same folder as your existing <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">aam.html</code>)</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>B. The Python script</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Create a folder called <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">scripts</code> if it doesn't exist</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Upload <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">fetch_aam_latlon.py</code> into the <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">scripts/</code> folder</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Final path: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">scripts/fetch_aam_latlon.py</code></li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>C. The GitHub Actions workflow</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Navigate to <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">.github/workflows/</code> (create it if needed via <strong>Add file â†’ Create new file</strong>, name it <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">.github/workflows/update_aam_lat.yml</code>)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Paste the contents of <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">update_aam_lat.yml</code> into that file and commit</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>D. Create the data folder placeholder</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <strong>Add file â†’ Create new file</strong></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Name it <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">data/aam_lat_latest.txt</code> (typing the slash auto-creates the folder)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Put a single line as placeholder content: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]"># placeholder â€” will be populated by GitHub Action</code></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Commit it â€” this lets Netlify deploy without a missing-file error</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Step 2 â€” Give the GitHub Action write permission</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The Action needs to commit the data file back to your repo.</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to your repo â†’ <strong>Settings</strong> â†’ <strong>Actions</strong> â†’ <strong>General</strong></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Scroll to <strong>Workflow permissions</strong></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Select <strong>Read and write permissions</strong></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Save</strong></li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Step 3 â€” Trigger the first run manually</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The first run downloads 31 years of base-period data and takes ~45â€“60 minutes. Do this once to seed the data file:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to your repo â†’ <strong>Actions</strong> tab</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Update Relative AAM (Latitude) Data</strong> in the left sidebar</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Run workflow</strong> â†’ <strong>Run workflow</strong> (green button)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Watch the logs â€” it will fetch 1980â€“2010 data, then recent years, then commit <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">data/aam_lat_latest.txt</code></li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">After this first run succeeds, every subsequent daily run only fetches the current year and takes ~2â€“3 minutes.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Step 4 â€” Verify the data file was written</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">After the Action completes:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to your repo's <strong>Code</strong> tab</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Open <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">data/aam_lat_latest.txt</code></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">You should see header lines starting with <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">#</code> followed by rows like:</li>
</ol>
