<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">If it still shows the placeholder, check the <strong>Actions</strong> logs for errors.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Step 5 â€” Netlify deploys automatically</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Since your Netlify site is already connected to this repo, it will auto-deploy when the Action commits the data file. No Netlify config changes needed. Your new page will be live at:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">https://phillyweatherauthorityaam.netlify.app/aam_hovmoller.html</code></strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">(or whatever your Netlify subdomain is â€” same pattern as your existing <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">aam.html</code>)</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Step 6 â€” Test it</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Open the URL above. You should see:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">The HovmÃ¶ller heatmap load with latitude on the Y-axis and time on the X-axis</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Red shading in the tropics during westerly periods, blue during easterly periods</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Contour lines at 0.5Ïƒ intervals</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">The range buttons (All / 1yr / 90d etc.) working to zoom the time axis</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">If you see a <strong>"Fetch error"</strong> message, it means either the data file is still a placeholder (Action hasn't run yet) or there's a path mismatch â€” double-check that <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">aam_lat_latest.txt</code> is in the <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">data/</code> folder.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Ongoing â€” it runs itself</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">After the first manual run, the GitHub Action fires every day at 06:30 UTC automatically. It fetches the latest NCEP/NCAR data, recomputes the anomalies, commits the updated file, and Netlify redeploys within a minute or two. Nothing else to do.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
